1. Definitions. "Software" — PupSeekRDP as source code, builds and docs.
"Modules" — paid features (see the License window and [price URL] for the
current list and prices). "Key" — a string unlocking Modules. "You" — the user.

2. Acceptance. Installing, building or using the Software means acceptance.
You confirm you are 18+ and legally capable (or act via a representative).
If you disagree — do not install, delete everything.

3. Permitted (non-exclusive, non-transferable; core — perpetual):
3.1. Use for any purpose, including commercial, on any number of your machines.
3.2. Read, study, modify the source for your own needs; build it for yourself.
3.3. The core (everything except Modules) is free forever.
3.4. By submitting a pull request or any code to the Rightholder you assign
all exclusive rights to it (modify, distribute, sublicense) free of charge
and warrant you are entitled to do so.

4. Prohibited without written consent:
4.1. Distributing the Software or modified versions in any form — except a
personal fork solely to review the code and submit pull requests; builds made
from a fork may not be distributed.
4.2. Bypassing, disabling or forging license/trial/module checks; sharing
bypass methods. 4.3. Using Modules without a Key and outside the trial.
4.4. Removing authorship notices; using the PupSeekRDP name; passing the code
off as your own. 4.5. Transferring the Key; one Key — one buyer.
4.6. Sublicensing or alienating the Software, rights or the Key.
4.7. Using the Software/code/texts/data for training AI/ML models, datasets,
or a competing product. 4.8. Reverse engineering beyond statutory exceptions.

5. Modules and payment. One-time payment = perpetual use of purchased Modules
(payment grants use, not code rights). A Key is reusable after reinstall.
Trial — 10 days, all Modules, once per user; wiping data or reinstalling does
not restart it. Refunds by agreement; statutory consumer rights unaffected.
The Rightholder may request proof of use (screenshot of the License window)
at most quarterly within 10 business days.

6. Updates/support as available, no deadlines; a new major version may bring a
new license. License text may be updated at [license URL]; your terms at
install/purchase time apply unless you accept the new ones.

7. Data. No collection, no telemetry, everything stays on your machine, the
Key is verified locally. Trial binding stores and compares only an irreversible
SHA256 hash of the machine id.

8. No warranties ("as is"). 9. Liability capped at amounts paid in the last
12 months (zero for free use); no lost profits. 10. Termination: breach ends
your rights; delete everything; clauses 4, 7–9 survive.
11. Governing law — Russian Federation; 30-day negotiation, then court at the
Rightholder's address. 12. Force majeure applies.
13. Severability; entire agreement; English is a translation, Russian prevails.
